    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "`solution.py` now implements `encode` and `decode` as spec'd, and `python -m pytest -q tests` passes with all 33 tests. I haven't seen the coverage, CRAP, mutation or bandit results, because I could only run the test command.\n\n`encode` groups runs with `itertools.groupby`. A run of 4 or more becomes `~n~c`. Shorter runs are written out literally, with each `~` doubled. `decode` is split into small helpers for reading the count and handling an escape, which keeps each function's complexity low. It raises `ValueError` for every malformed case in the spec. It still accepts well-formed text that `encode` wouldn't produce, such as plain `\"aaaa\"`.\n\nThe tests in `tests/test_solution.py` cover:\n- encoding and decoding round trips, including runs of `~` and non-ASCII characters;\n- the lenient decode cases;\n- 16 malformed inputs that must raise `ValueError`.",
